Installed-Size: 541
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.38), libglib2.0-0t64 (>= 2.79.0), libgusb2 (>= 0.2.4), libssl3t64 (>= 3.0.0), fprintd, libfprint-2-2, libpam-fprintd, libglib2.0-bin, libnotify-bin, usbutils, systemd, polkitd, pkexec, python3, python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-fprint-2.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/david-bartlett/fingerprint-fix-sdcp
Description: Egis fingerprint reader fix for Samsung Galaxy Book
 Makes the Egis match-on-chip fingerprint reader (1c7a:05a5 on Galaxy Book 4 /
 Book 5 Pro, 1c7a:05a1 on Book 3 / Book 4) work on Linux. Builds only the
 egismoc SDCP driver of libfprint and points fprintd at it; the distro's
 libfprint is not replaced.
 .
 Includes a monitor and boot-time check that warn when the sensor loses a
 fingerprint (e.g. after booting Windows), sharing enrolments between installs,
 and the Galaxy Book Fingerprint Manager.
